# Normalise line endings to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# The instruction set is compiled into the binary with go:embed. A CRLF
# checkout would embed CRLF documents, seed them into a vault, and then fail to
# recognise them: reading a note back normalises the line endings away, so the
# stored seed fingerprint could never match and every shipped document would
# report as modified for ever. That is exactly what happened on Windows CI.
* text=auto eol=lf
